# S5-07 canonical initramfs marker-order N=2

Date: 2026-11-16

## Purpose

Run the current strict automatic N=2 `stage4-init-nonce` series using the
canonical Stage 4 initramfs after moving its existing checked 1 ms sleep before
the nonce write. This uses the original 3,000,000,000-retirement profile and
the opt-in schema-v5 execution-observation sidecars. The marker parser,
comparator, and acceptance rules are unchanged.

## Provenance and command

`od-runner` was rebuilt from commit `b6d5e78` with
`cargo build -p od-runner --release --offline`; binary SHA-256:
`d0e3be4b345cb1ce4b2b5e72c721630ab098641b29e77816b13fdd2e13c4251f`.
The build succeeded with the existing `page_walk.rs:1219` dead-code warning.

```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --test-runs 2 \
  --series-id stage5-s5-07-canonical-pre-marker-sleep-n2-20261116-a \
  --scenario-id stage4-init-nonce \
  --expected-stop-kind budget_exhausted \
  --out work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-canonical-pre-marker-sleep-n2-20261116-a/series.json \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --ram-mib 128 --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 \
  --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode --execution-observations
```

The profile did not use `--linux-norandmaps`. Each input hash was identical
between runs:

| Input | SHA-256 |
|---|---|
| Linux 7.0.0-38-generic kernel | `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e` |
| Canonical initramfs | `65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7` |
| CPU0 ACPI blob | `6fc25b091348d8ad314bdd0f4f579ec9dd3969c961020a7a61d2daeb8dc26d4d` |
| ACPI manifest | `2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2` |

The canonical fixture `init.S` SHA-256 is
`1b40a651a80acd8f203f2d3a21c76d06fc7000f8084428b72d5735998b7784c7`.

## Results

| Run | Scenario | Marker | Retired / stop | Delivered #PF | CPL0 RDTSC total | UART bytes / SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|
| 0001 | passed | exact and valid | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | 34 | 34,401,050 | 24,086 / `258712baddb16fbbba892e77a2c9aae7cf2422aa6126f6f1f1c8bed0f8c4519b` |
| 0002 | passed | exact and valid | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | 34 | 34,424,800 | 24,002 / `3ebe789ac812bf48a47e92c7ed05835cb03fbfe4a978907c84017bfe270d1dbd` |

Both UARTs contain separate lines in the expected order:

```text
[    2.271132] Run /init as init process
OD_NONCE=OD518e878f3f96ffdf800012fdc00000000

[    2.271102] Run /init as init process
OD_NONCE=OD518e87a00efc97e3800012fdc00000001
```

The automatic series reports `outcome=passed` for both guest scenarios, but
the command exits 1 because strict comparison returns `matches=false`. Its
unexplained fields remain `run[1].machine_observations` and
`run[1].ordered_uart_bytes` after the existing nonce normalization.

Each schema-v5 sidecar retained all 34 #PF records, 22 CPL0 RDTSC sites, and
reported zero omitted faults, site overflow, and unattributed RDTSC reads. The
first 30 #PF signatures match; event 30 has the same RIP
`0xffffffff8271a9c1` and error code `0x2` but different CR2 stack addresses
(`0x7ffd28785499` and `0x7ffc0f3286a9`); the remaining three signatures match.
RDTSC differs by 23,750 reads across eight sites. The largest delta is 23,649
reads at RIP `0xffffffff8271b34d`, previously resolved against the matching
kernel debug ELF as `delay_tsc+0x4d` ([prior symbol mapping](s5-07-current-acpi-sidecars-n2-20261116.log)).
These are observations, not an explanation or a classification as benign. UART
lengths and hashes also differ; the first ordered differences occur among
kernel boot messages around 0.35–0.38 seconds. Sidecar overhead was not
isolated, so no performance comparison is claimed.

The canonical fixture reproduces the two clean nonce lines at the original
budget, eliminating the previous marker-validation failure in this pair. The
strict machine and UART variation remains, so S5-07 is still blocked/unaccepted.

